{"kind":"assert","text":"Planner planning correction of R2 revision2, exact head f146aa2ef1f77775b49ec2f07c47f5879f978e42, handoff3265ebe. I read the complete revised main note1121 lines84087 bytes,SHA-25677ca6209ee61404d7d5eee83b0d1d9f3356ce3e8ec6396bd20f8338f2665e62d; the full correction matrix25 lines7274 bytes,SHA-25611c263986b0d7c3b4b600f36c8a95a209cd0343c327abb6e99c1676de630b457; and the entire revised documentation evidence533 lines75516 bytes,SHA-25619901c1851a6c842776cfb8efd2165f395a613715e5fa49c61a3debfbe84d17f. The three-file revision diff passes whitespace checking. I checked only two bounded official-page details again today, Findings and reader expansion of hidden comments; I did not refetch or independently reverify all240 documentation rows or compare screens.\n\nThe stable conditions fact, explicit report-under binding, attribution of the actual commitment, comment/verdict separation, same-manifest check retry, commitment-specific forks, intended-state freeze, tombstone-aware redaction coverage, qualified direct private reads and complete Jam timing outcome address much of5f83a4bf. Six focused corrections remain. No implementation or runtime work is authorized.\n\n1. Preserve uncertainty between sending and receipt, including expiry. Section10.1.1 and the matrix currently say closing a device before received/admitted means nothing started, and expired means nothing happened. Counterexample: the service admitted the task or control, but its reply was lost before the browser closed; notAfter then passed. The task may now be running and must appear on enrolled device B. Distinguish provably never-dispatched local queue entries from sent/unacknowledged intents. For the latter, ask for settlement with the exact signed bytes even after expiry/revocation; return an existing receipt without re-admission, or report outcome still unknown/unavailable. Only a definitive settlement answer that no admission exists under the owning scope's retained history, with no remaining admissible delivery, can support 'expired without admission'; a local clock or absent client receipt cannot. Use 'checking whether work started' while uncertain, never 'No work has started'. Show lost reply before close/expired unsent queue/accepted before expiry but learned later in compact sequences. Received/queued is already a durable task admission; applied needs its distinct correlated runtime outcome. Device B sees authoritative task state even if A never saw its receipt. No silent re-signing or unsafe side-effect repetition.\n\n2. Bind complete work to the actual goal, plan, concerns and accepted terms, and keep failures in the required set. Section5.2 does not yet check that the named goal conditions fact belongs to the plan's issue and equals the plan's conditionsAt; that each resolve-concern decision is about this exact plan's required concern; or that its replacement and the selected acceptance/report are those it names. A same-issue decision about another plan must not discharge this one. State duplicate/ambiguous selection handling and the exact report→commitment→accepted conditions/parties chain, including a child's renegotiated terms and a recorded parent decision when those no longer cover the planned purpose. The seal-plan rule currently lists only created/delivered children, silently omitting refused/conflict required concerns. Preserve the required concern identity and outcome until an authorized recorded exclusion/replacement, rather than making that failed work vanish from coverage. Define alternative roles consistently with the frozen required/optional lists. A no-plan single-person change remains legitimate, but omitting an existing required plan must not be an integrator-controlled shortcut to 'complete'; define the owner's exact recorded no-plan/supersession/coverage decision and its subject, without imposing decomposition on ordinary single-person fixes. Either designate one current plan under an explicit rule or qualify the assertion 'two plans never run together'; open-plan currently permits several. Historical plans/commitments remain immutable, and no guard polls a foreign child's present state.\n\n3. Finish parent-result and inherited-contribution provenance. R1 relationship revisions are per owner/item. Two fulfilled commitments in one child have different owner items, so keeping each item's maximum does not stop a delayed first commitment result from overwriting the parent's one concern.result after the second arrived. Retain results per commitment and derive a current presentation under a defined child-owned revision, or use one stable child/concern relationship identity; state exact correlation and both delivery orders. Do not compare positions of different child scopes. Similarly, use-input can incorporate an accepted report into later work, while the later report authors currently include only its own commitment history. Define how the consumed input's exact report/acceptance and attribution stay in the later report/manifest, or forbid hiding that input from the selected contribution closure. A former author must not become eligible to review their own incorporated contribution by reporting it through a different commitment. Add the required R1 form as a named gap if necessary. Keep manual close, fulfilled commitment, accepted report, requester judgment and actual published Git outcome separate.\n\n4. Make retryable jobs and ownership guards executable in the declared model. The job table marks passed/failed as final, while request-check transitions those jobs to superseded; R1 says final items refuse every transition. Make those states nonfinal under precise supersession guards, or keep immutable result/job records with an explicit current-selection mechanism. Bind the earlier review/job item to the same reviewer/member, manifest and job name; naming somebody else's earlier verdict must not let a signer supersede it. request-check must use the grant/definition-qualified checker and exact issued job/config/tree/attempt contract from R3, not any checker-role signature. The apparent P.27 duplicate must distinguish a new independently signed answer from retransmission of identical signed bytes: the latter returns the original receipt and opens no result entry. Complete shorthand own/any rows with their actual grant and signer guard on the named author/requester, including ready/to-draft, review requests, link/unlink and close/reopen; a role's own-action grant alone is not a party check. Name every local item read or changed as an atomic subject with expected revisions, including proposal, earlier review, review-request and manifest selectors, or declare the needed grammar gap; don't claim every row already does this while several read unlisted items. Use R1's resolved-identity alias checks. Record exact new counts/limits as proposals, not a requirement for new test matrices.\n\n5. Reconcile publication progress and frozen eligibility with R3's correctionf6c4d14b. R1's one-terminal-result request protocol and R3's repeated reserved/unresolved/published results conflict; this draft inherits it. Use the jointly chosen correlated request/progress/final protocol with destination identity/incarnation/owner revisions, wrong-target refusal, out-of-order handling and once-only closure effects. Once published, an older reserved/unresolved update must not revert the state. Eligibility must include the complete pinned live reviews/check-job selection and blocking request-changes, not an arbitrary counted subset. Late check output during intended/committed cannot silently mutate frozen eligibility; state its retained/queued/refused-retry path without rerunning the external job to manufacture an answer. Description/link disagreement is acceptable only as the deliberately visible staged client flow already chosen; state whether a pending mismatch blocks merge or whether merge explicitly names/shows the actual frozen link set, so a person cannot interpret unrecorded Closes text as a guaranteed recorded closure. Keep revocation/read-session/stream grace and direct owner/admin private control consistent with the corrected R3 proof/lifecycle. Report after a fulfilled final commitment requires successor work, not an illegal reopen.\n\n6. Finish the few evidence/presentation distinctions. A reader expanding a collapsed comment is a local presentation action; changing the authoritative collapsed→visible state remains the granted expand-comment act. The page should not require a moderator grant just to see readable collapsed text. The issue/PR body and review/report-summary redaction are promised but only comment redaction acts are defined: name their concrete permitted actions and field/revision/tombstone/retention rules, or mark them as an explicit scoped follow-up rather than claiming the initial complete workflow includes unspecified controls. R1/R3/R4 still own authenticated removal proof, secrets scanned at admission, owned payload deletion and retained backup/export/unknown-duty pins; do not claim complete semantic replay when bytes cannot be derived. The official pull-request reference https://docs.github.com/en/pull-requests/reference/pull-requests says Findings includes automated code-review results, giving code-scanning alerts as an example; section11.4/evidence13.20 should not narrow it to only code scanning or infer the whole tab's plan availability from the example. Keep the initial deferral and honest no-screen-parity qualification. Reader expansion is explicitly supported by https://docs.github.com/en/communities/moderating-comments-and-conversations/managing-disruptive-comments. Amend only these bounded summaries/links; no entire-corpus refetch is requested.\n\nReturn a corrected exact head and matrix before independent design review. Cross-draft choices stay named and unadopted; the browser story, real cloud workspace, device continuity, useful-invariant10× test economy and whole Artroom application/compone